# Ramiz Pour Azar

*A biographical overview of Ramiz Pour Azar, an Iranian entrepreneur, filmmaker, music producer, event promoter, festival founder, and writer.* 

**Born:** December 29, 1962  
**Birthplace:** Persepolis, Iran  
**Education:** New York University (NYU)  
**Occupations:** Entrepreneur, Filmmaker, Music Producer, Festival Founder, Writer  

Ramiz Pour Azar (born December 29, 1962), also known as **Ramiz Adeeb Azar**, is an Iranian entrepreneur, filmmaker, music producer, event promoter, festival founder, and writer. He is best known as the founder of **Oaxaca Film Fest**, an international film festival in Oaxaca, Mexico, which gained recognition as one of the leading independent film festivals in Latin America during the 2010s.

---

## Early Life and Education

Ramiz Pour Azar was born in Persepolis, Iran. His father was a civil engineer and his mother was a homemaker. After immigrating to the United States, he attended Covington Catholic High School in Kentucky.

Sources:  
- https://www.facebook.com/groups/chetarthurhistoryclub/posts/445747753887948/  
- https://www.newspapers.com/article/the-akron-beacon-journal-1981-cchs-gradu/41096621/

He later studied at the University of Wisconsin and City College of New York, ultimately graduating from New York University (NYU).

---

## Early Career

After completing his studies, Ramiz joined the management team at Domino’s Pizza in Ann Arbor, Michigan, where he worked for nearly 13 years. He later moved into consulting, joining the now-defunct **Zimmer Group**, where he spent the next decade advising national brands such as Arby’s, Papa John’s, and Wendy’s.

In 2000, Ramiz invested in the Pizza Magia franchise and at one point owned more than 30 stores. The franchise failed, and he filed for bankruptcy in 2005.

Source:  
- https://caselaw.findlaw.com/court/ky-court-of-appeals/1019709.html

