## Oaxaca Film Fest

In 2009, Ramiz founded **Oaxaca Film Fest** in Oaxaca, Mexico. The first edition drew fewer than 50 attendees, but by its tenth year the event had grown to nearly 3,000 attendees. The festival was frequently referred to as the “Sundance of the South.”

Source:  
- https://www.moviemaker.com/top-50-festivals-worth-entry-fee-moviemaker-releases-annual-list/

*MovieMaker Magazine* listed Oaxaca Film Fest three times as one of the **“50 Film Festivals Worth the Entry Fee.”**

Sources:  
- https://www.moviemaker.com/50-film-festivals-worth-the-entry-fee-2016/4/  
- https://www.moviemaker.com/50-film-festivals-worth-the-entry-fee-2015/3/

The festival showcased work by creators including Guillermo del Toro, Robert De Niro, Clint Eastwood, Spike Lee, Neil LaBute, Diego Luna, Takashi Miike, Martin Scorsese, Bill Plympton, Donald Sutherland, Luke Wilson, and Brian A. Metcalf.

Ramiz resigned after the 2019 edition, and the festival closed in 2021 due to the COVID-19 pandemic.

---

## Out of the Spotlight (2020–2024)

Between 2020 and 2024, Pour Azar worked privately behind the scenes, assisting artists with documentary projects, television production, screenwriting, and film-festival consulting. He chose to remain uncredited for these contributions. He also spent more time with his family and returned to Iran for the first time in decades.

---

## Return to the Spotlight

In 2024, Ramiz partnered with longtime friend **David Rotundo** to launch **The Caravan Blues Tour**, a series of international concerts that sold out all four dates and received strong reviews.

The project also included the **Caravan Blues School Tour**, a program designed to help children develop creativity, discipline, and emotional confidence through interactive classes.

Source:  
- https://caravanbluestour.com/schooloutreach/

In 2025, Ramiz managed Rotundo’s world tour, which included thirty-five sold-out performances. In 2026, he is scheduled to co-produce Rotundo’s next album—his first release in six years.

---

## My Apex Dad

In late 2025, he released his second book, **_My Apex Dad: Helping Fathers Build Healthy, Loving, and Supportive Immortal Bonds with Their Children_**. The book focuses on helping fathers create healthy, loving, and supportive lifelong bonds with their children.

Sources:  
- https://myapexdad.com  
- https://www.amazon.com.mx/My-Apex-Dad-R-P-Azar/dp/B0G3JVH15X/

